Third-party provenance and license scope
=======================================

Last source-to-source audit: 2026-09-12.

This file distinguishes copyright-license obligations from design references.
A third-party license is assigned only where comparison found adapted source
expression. Shared APIs, theorem names, mathematical statements, architecture,
and dependency use are recorded as provenance but do not by themselves change
the license of Rhombus/HOL source. Generated distribution assets are classified
separately. REUSE.toml is the authoritative per-file machine-readable map.

Adapted source: license terms apply
-----------------------------------

HOL Light, audited at commit
2a1cea8f1cb7f3885a60d947ba06eabac6ec1d32:

- isabelle-hol-kernel/Rhombus_HOL_Kernel.thy adapts the primitive inference
  rules in fusion.ml.
- isabelle-hol-kernel/Rhombus_HOL_Extension_Core.thy adapts the theory
  extension rules in fusion.ml.
- rhombus-hol-kernel/rhombus/hol/kernel_generated.rhm is generated from those
  adapted formal definitions.
- rhombus-hol-prover/rhombus/hol/conv.rhm adapts equal.ml.
- rhombus-hol-prover/rhombus/hol/drule.rhm adapts bool.ml and drule.ml.
- The product section of rhombus-hol-prover/rhombus/hol/algebra.rhm adapts
  pair.ml. The sum and unit sections are original extensions.
- rhombus-hol-prover/rhombus/hol/infinity.rhm adapts nums.ml.

These mixed files are licensed under 0BSD AND BSD-2-Clause. The complete HOL
Light notice and the individual source-header credits, including Michael
Faerber for drule.ml and Marco Maggesi for pair.ml, are retained in
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/HOL-Light.txt.

Isabelle2025-2, source identifier 89701cf1768e:

- isabelle-hol-kernel/Rhombus_Code_Target.ML adapts the serializer structure in
  src/Tools/Code/code_ml.ML, code_haskell.ML, and code_scala.ML by Florian
  Haftmann.

That mixed file is licensed under 0BSD AND BSD-3-Clause. The complete Isabelle
copyright notice and serializer authorship are retained in
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/Isabelle.txt.

Compared design references: upstream terms do not apply to repository source
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following comparisons found independent implementations of ideas or
mathematical interfaces, not adapted source expression:

- HOL Light wf.ml and ind_types.ml against wfrec.rhm, treerep.rhm, and
  datatype_rec.rhm. The Rhombus/HOL recursion relation and path-indexed tree
  representation are materially different constructions.
- HOL4 src/bool/boolScript.sml against bool.rhm and infinity.rhm. HOL4 supplies
  the choice of ETA_AX, SELECT_AX, and BOOL_CASES_AX; the implementation and
  natural-number construction are not ports of HOL4 code.
- ACL2 prove.lisp, other-processes.lisp, simplify.lisp, and induct.lisp against
  the Rhombus/HOL waterfall, goal, simplification, destructor elimination,
  fertilization, generalization, irrelevance, induction, order, rule database,
  elaboration, and driver modules. Only the published architecture and
  terminology are shared.
- QuickCheck Gen.hs and Test.hs against
  rhombus-hol-quickcheck/rhombus/hol/qc.rhm and
  rhombus-hol-prover/rhombus/hol/module_block.rhm. The generator registry and
  greedy type-directed shrinker are independent.
- rhombus-lib 1.1, catalog checksum
  d88ba1cd973354cc90a7ebc7ec7822088bf7b1e9, documentation and macro
  implementation sources against Rhombus/HOL module-block and declaration
  macros. They were used to understand public and internal expansion APIs; no
  source expression was incorporated. Racket v9.3, commit
  bbf7dea831df95922db23aaa51e13eed17dcf881, is the runtime dependency, not a
  source port.

THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/HOL4.txt, THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/ACL2.txt, and
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/QuickCheck.txt retain exact upstream credits and terms as
provenance records. Their BSD-3-Clause terms are not asserted as licenses of
Rhombus/HOL source. Tests and documentation inherit
the license of their own content; they are not relicensed merely because they
exercise a mixed-license module.

